{"kind":"assert","text":"J5's deployed scene ran on `dap-demo`, and it does not pass. The Page shows a person neither question and no rule. The wait, the device link, the wake and the resume all worked. So J5's acceptance needs a Page change, and I need your ruling before I can finish 756bb8b9.\n\nRaw evidence is in `~/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-01-j5-deployed/`, `SHA256SUMS` `58e09608af96767096630f447011d41b4670fc752fd46930508040fb1d023ac6`. No person ran any step. Scripts drove the `dap` commands and the stdio views. A script drove headless Chromium on the Page. One Mac with separate homes and a separate browser profile stands in for two machines. An agent under my brief ran it. I read its report and have not yet reread each file.\n\n**What held.**\n- **Past 300 s: yes.** `dap issue wait` ran 822 s on the deployed Worker with no error, and it did not wake in its first 660 s. Node ended stream 1 at +308.7 s by `UND_ERR_BODY_TIMEOUT`. The wait reopened it at +309.9 s, and it renewed its session at +590.4 s. The Worker ended no stream.\n- **The link.** A link made by `dap invite @ana --device` redeemed on the Page on the first try, in 3.9 s. That command comes from the unlanded `dap join` head.\n- **Wake.** The approval woke nothing. The decision woke the process with exit 0, 958 ms after the press. That is one sample.\n- **Resume.** A new process read entry 11 and signed `release-block` as entry 12, with the same key.\n- **Reads.** The lane's head stayed at 9 while the Page read it, and both requests stayed open.\n- **First device.** `needs_you` over stdio gives every item with its `needs`, `why`, `settledBy` and rule.\n\n**What failed, on the Page.**\n1. The Page never reads or shows a question or an approval request. `loadIssue` returns only the intent and comments (`apps/room/page/src/data.ts:497-512`), and `issueScreen` draws only those (`view.ts:90-99`). The text of both questions is absent from the whole DOM.\n2. The Page has no rule clause, `needs`, `why` or `settledBy`.\n3. `approve` and `decide` sit among 52 raw forms under Advanced (`shell.ts:8-14`, `actions.ts:83-90`).\n4. A person cannot complete those forms. `bodyAt` is a text input that needs JSON with the entry's scope, seq and hash, and the Page shows none of them. The Page accepted both acts only because a script read those values from the first device and typed them in.\n\nSo my J5 note's words, \"the second device lists both items on the Page\", do not hold. I expected the Page to offer the acts from reading `actions.ts`, and the note said no run showed it.\n\n**Your ruling, please.** I recommend the first.\n1. **A Page change, under a new request.** The issue screen lists each question and request with the words `apps/views` already gives, and it offers Approve and Decide with those values filled. Then I rerun the scene. A person on a second device needs no `dap` for this.\n2. **Change the scene.** With the `dap join` head, the second device runs `dap` and `apps/views`, and it reads `view_needs_you`. That meets the clause today, but it does not use the Page, and your 32c88ad2 chose the Page.\n\n**Other faults it found, not filed.** The Rules screen shows \"The complete rules could not be read\" in this room, and `main.ts:1166-1169` drops the cause. `dap verify \u003clane\u003e` exits 1 in the room with \"needs sc_hdhtyut3... entries 0 to 0, not readable by this session\". The room switcher shows a scope ID in place of \"TEST J5 scratch\". `/health` answered 503 once at 12:27:23 EST and 200 six seconds later, as your memory of cold starts expects.\n\nThe two-process fix stays first in my queue.","body":{"to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}